<Base title="About — Trypup" description="What Trypup is, why it exists and how it helps you make a responsible decision about getting a dog. And if you already have a dog, how it helps you care for it." lang="en" alt="/o-aplikaci/" pageKey="about">
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <h1 data-cms="about.en.title">About the app</h1>
    <p class="meta" data-cms="about.en.meta">Dog on trial · a responsible decision · Dog at home</p>

    <p data-cms="about.en.intro"><strong>Trypup is an educational dog-care simulator for anyone seriously considering getting a real dog — adults and families with children alike.</strong> The goal is to reduce the number of dogs in shelters by getting people to think BEFORE they decide — not after. Since version 2.0, Trypup also helps people who already have a dog, in Dog at home mode.</p>

    <h2 data-cms="about.en.whyTitle">Why Trypup exists</h2>
    <p data-cms="about.en.whyText">Dogs mostly end up in shelters not because of their temperament, but because of their owners' circumstances — time, money, housing, life changes. Trypup walks you through the daily routine as a dry run, with no consequences for a living animal.</p>

    <h2>Dog on trial: how it works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Starting questionnaire</strong> — recommends a breed based on your lifestyle.</li>
      <li><strong>30-day challenge</strong> — after 30 days you get an evaluation and a short final quiz. If you'd rather skip the challenge, choose Classic care (“For life”).</li>
      <li><strong>Daily care</strong> — feeding, play, grooming, rest; the dog's stats react to your care.</li>
      <li><strong>GPS walks</strong> — real routes with time and distance, and a check that you actually went out.</li>
      <li><strong>Training</strong> — 9 commands with progressive unlocks; each breed learns differently.</li>
      <li><strong>Health & costs</strong> — vaccination schedule and estimated monthly and yearly costs, based on Czech prices (converted).</li>
      <li><strong>Education</strong> — articles on adoption, choosing a shelter and care, quizzes and “True or myth?” for each breed.</li>
      <li><strong>When care falls short</strong> — neglect the dog for several days and it goes to a shelter, and the app explains what it was missing. With no consequences for a living animal.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Dog at home: for your real dog</h2>
    <p>Already have a dog? Choose “I already have a dog” when you first open the app, or turn on Dog at home mode any time in Settings under “How you use Trypup”.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Care plan and reminders</strong> — vaccinations, deworming, tick and flea protection, a preventive health check, plus your own reminders, such as a dog tax where one applies; you can add a date to your calendar.</li>
      <li><strong>Diary</strong> — vet visits, vaccinations, medication, weight, symptoms, walks and training in one place.</li>
      <li><strong>Dog passport</strong> — microchip, your dog's details and contacts for pet sitters. A digital copy; it doesn't replace the official passport.</li>
      <li><strong>Vet and first aid</strong> — your home vet one tap away, the nearest vet or a 24/7 emergency vet on the map, and advice on what to do right away if your dog eats something poisonous.</li>
      <li><strong>Sharing</strong> — send an overview for a pet sitter, one for a vet, or the full copy as text.</li>
      <li><strong>Names and name days</strong> — help choosing a name, and reminders of your dog's name day, birthday and the anniversary of coming home.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>One dog is free; Premium is there for more dogs. Your dogs' data never gets locked, not even after Premium ends.</p>
    <p><strong>Trypup does not replace a vet.</strong> If you have any doubt about your dog's health, call your vet.</p>

    <h2 data-cms="about.en.breedsTitle">Breeds</h2>
    <p data-cms="about.en.breedsText">For the dog on trial, four breeds are free — one of each size (small, medium, large) plus the Shelter Mix — and more are available as Premium (Border Collie, Siberian Husky, German Shepherd, Golden Retriever, Bernese Mountain Dog and others).</p>

    <h2 data-cms="about.en.commitTitle">Our commitment</h2>
    {/* Věta o věnování části výnosů útulkům je JEN v české verzi (rozhodnutí zakladatele 2. 10. 2026) —
